OpenSE4's changes to MicroPython 1.29.0 (tools/update_micropython.sh applies them).
They add hooks that the script runtime's port (src/script/port) fills in; with the
hooks left at their defaults MicroPython behaves as before.

- Budget: MICROPY_VM_HOOK_OPCODE runs before every bytecode (py/vm.c). Native work
  that has no bytecode of its own is charged with MICROPY_BUDGET_CHARGE (C-level
  iteration in py/runtime.c, big-number multiplication, division and conversion in
  py/mpz.c, regular expression backtracking in extmod/modre.c, substring search in
  py/objstr.c) or, where raising mid-change would be unsafe, MICROPY_BUDGET_DEBIT
  (hash collisions in py/map.c). Big-integer work is charged only beyond 64 bits,
  where every word size uses big integers alike.
- Call depth: MICROPY_CALL_DEPTH_CHECK/ENTER/EXIT around the execution of bytecode
  functions and generators (py/objfun.c, py/objgenerator.c).
- Hashes the same on every platform: integers (small or big) and whole-valued floats
  hash as their value modulo MICROPY_HASH_INT_MODULUS (py/runtime.c, py/mpz.c,
  py/mpz.h, py/objint_mpz.c, py/objfloat.c); every hash is limited by MICROPY_HASH_MASK; tuples, frozensets and
  bound methods hash from their parts, never from an address (py/objtuple.c,
  py/objset.c, py/objboundmeth.c).
- Object identity without addresses: MICROPY_OBJ_IDENTITY for hash() of objects
  without a value hash, MICROPY_OBJ_ID_VALUE for id() of objects and interned
  strings, an identity field in class instances set from MICROPY_OBJ_NEW_IDENTITY
  (py/objtype.h, py/objtype.c, py/obj.c), and MICROPY_PRINT_POINTER_VALUE for "%p"
  in reprs (py/mpprint.c).
- MICROPY_PORT_IMPORT_LOAD lets the port supply a module's compiled code, e.g. from
  a cache (py/builtinimport.c).
- MICROPY_MAP_INSERTION_ORDER: dicts, instance attributes and module globals keep
  their keys in insertion order, as in CPython, with their hashes stored and an
  index beside the entries (py/map.c, py/obj.h; dict.copy and dict.popitem in
  py/objdict.c).
- MICROPY_COMP_CLASS_ANNOTATIONS: annotated names in a class body are recorded,
  in order, in the class's __annotations__ as short texts (py/compile.c,
  py/scope.h), so that dataclasses can find their fields.
- MICROPY_PY_MATH_EXTENSIBLE makes math an extensible built-in, so that a math.py
  can add functions to it (py/modmath.c).
- MICROPY_PY_DICT_UPDATE_FROM_SUBCLASS: dict(x) and d.update(x) read a Python
  subclass of dict (defaultdict, Counter) as a dict (py/objdict.c).
- MICROPY_MACHINE_INT_32: conversions of ints to machine words (sizes, indices,
  range() bounds) accept 32-bit values on every word size (py/obj.c,
  py/objstrunicode.c); struct, array and int.to_bytes still take whole small ints
  (py/binary.c, py/objint_mpz.c); range lengths and steps can't overflow a 32-bit
  word (py/objrange.c).
- MICROPY_LIST_SORT lets the port provide list.sort (py/objlist.c).
- MICROPY_PY_BUILTINS_OPEN leaves out open() while keeping io's in-memory streams
  (py/modbuiltins.c, py/modio.c).
- MICROPY_FLOAT_C_FUN may be defined by the port (py/mpconfig.h); MP_SYS_MAXSIZE
  sets sys.maxsize (py/objint_mpz.c); MICROPY_NATIVE_LONG_SIZE sets the size of the
  native 'l' and 'L' codes of struct and array (py/binary.c).

